ts. To maximize scoring potential, forming additional Pungs (e.g., T3 or B9) or Chows in Characters is critical. Discarding a non-vital tile like B8 preserves key tiles for potential Pungs in T3/B9 and avoids disrupting the Characters sequence.  \\nReason: B8 is a single tile with no immediate meld utility. Discarding it maintains flexibility for forming Pungs (T3/B9) and preserves the Characters sequence (W3-W6) for potential Chows. Keeping T3 and B9 increases chances of completing high-value Pungs, while B8\\u2019s discard minimizes risk of losing critical tiles.  \\nAnswer: Play B8\"}"}
