ain the potential for forming two chows in the W suit, leading to an All Chows pattern (2 points) and a structured hand.]\nReason: [Discarding W9 preserves the W3, W4, W5, and W6 tiles, which can form two chows (W3-4-5 and W4-5-6). This structure, combined with a pair of T3 or B9, creates a valid hand with All Chows (2 points) and avoids disrupting potential melds. Other discards risk breaking chows or reducing scoring opportunities.]\nAnswer: Play W9"}
