esn't lead to a valid hand structure. Passing is safer.\nReason: Forming a Chow with T4 (T3, T4, T5) would leave remaining tiles that cannot form two additional melds and a pair. The hand structure remains incomplete, so passing avoids unnecessary risks.\nAnswer: Pass"}
